xpansion-game-changing-updates-for-a-resort-in-need","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"How do I get to Steamboat?","a":"**The terrain in numbers:** **~3,741 permitted acres**, **182 trails**, a **3,668 ft vertical**, and **23 lifts** (2 gondolas, a six-pack, quads) — terrain split ~**14% beginner / 42% intermediate / 44% advanced**, plus ~30 acres of night skiing.","source":"https://www.steamboat.com/the-mountain/mountain-stats","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Steamboat?","a":"Ski Champagne Powder off the Wild Blue Gondola — ride North America''s longest/fastest gondola to Sunshine Peak and drop into Steamboat''s trademark dry, light Champagne Powder — the signature Steamboat run.","source":"https://www.peakrankings.com/content/steamboat-wild-blue-gondola-stage-ii-and-mahogany-ridge-expansion-game-changing-updates-for-a-resort-in-need","accessed":"2026-07-18"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Steamboat Ski Guide: Champagne Powder, a Ranching Town & Natural Hot Springs","meta_description":"Plan Steamboat, Colorado - ''Ski Town USA'': trademarked Champagne Powder on Mount Werner (~3,741 acres, the new Wild Blue Gondola), a real Western ranching town, genuine natural hot springs (Strawberry Park + Old Town), Steamboat Powdercats cat-skiing and the 1914 Winter Carnival, on the Ikon Pass, with real timing, altitude/avalanche safety and booking intel.","slug":"steamboat-colorado","primary_keyword":"Steamboat Colorado travel guide","long_tail":["Steamboat Champagne Powder skiing","Strawberry Park Hot Springs winter","Steamboat cat skiing Buffalo Pass","Wild Blue Gondola Steamboat","Steamboat Winter Carnival","Steamboat Ikon Pass"],"search_language":"es-US","local_keywords":["guia de viaje Steamboat Colorado","Champagne Powder Steamboat","aguas termales Strawberry Park","cat-skiing Buffalo Pass","Winter Carnival Steamboat","Steamboat Ikon Pass"],"hreflang":["en","es-US"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-18","attribution":{"author":{"ty