  ('summit-at-snoqualmie-washington', '12A', 'The Summit at Snoqualmie', 'United States', 'Seattle''s home mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Pacific Northwest', '{"ski","family","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Closest major ski area to Seattle — ~52 mi/~1 hr E on I-90 at Snoqualmie Pass (~3,000 ft base)","Boyne Resorts-owned (since March 2018); Ikon Pass partner destination (5-7 Ikon days) + own local Alpental Plus season pass (from ~$459)","Four base areas — Summit West, Summit Central, Summit East, Alpental; combined ~1,914 acres, 62 trails, 20 chairlifts + 5 surface lifts, ~435 in avg snowfall","Alpental = 2,280 ft vertical (base ~2,610 ft / top ~5,420 ft) — steepest/most serious + backcountry terrain in the state","Largest night skiing in America (~541 lit acres, to 10 p.m.); Summit Tubing Center (20 lanes); 50+ km Nordic; summer bike park (opened 2022)","Consolidated under one management from 1997; day/night commuter mountain (minimal on-mountain lodging; metro/North Bend base)","2026-27 Alpental Plus blackouts: Dec 26 2026-Jan 1 2027 + Sat/Sun Jan 2-Feb 28 2027 + Jan 18 + Feb 16 2027 (verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"Nearest 24/7 ER: Snoqualmie Valley Hospital (Snoqualmie, ~30-40 min W on I-90, serves pass to North Bend); larger at Swedish Issaquah (~45 min W) + Seattle trauma (Harborview, regional Level I); serious cases transfer to Seattle; backcountry via King/Kittitas county SAR / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"WSDOT I-90 Snoqualmie Pass driving + chain control + winter-long avalanche control (roadway closures, artillery, 30 min-several hr delays); AVALANCHE — Alpental in-area steeps + serious sidecountry/backcountry Back Bowls (NWAC bulletin, guide + beacon/probe/shovel beyond ropes); heavy maritime ''Cascade Concrete'' + tree-well/snow-immersion + rain-on-snow icy patches at low base; night-ski low light + wind-hold (Alpental). Altitude LOW (base ~3,000 ft) — AMS not a concern","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, Feb) + every weekend AND most weeknights (Seattle-metro commuter mountain; after-work night sessions + family Saturdays sharpest); powder days spike Alpental","shoulder":"early season (early-mid Dec), Jan weekdays, late Mar-Apr spring value; Nordic + tubing carry non-alpine demand","green":"May-mid Nov (alpine closed; summer bike park + disc golf + scenic lift + I-90 hiking carry modest green season)","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + peak-weekend beds 2-5 mo; ordinary weekends 1-6 wk; weeknight night-ski + tubing days-ahead/same-week; season passes (Alpental Plus/Ikon) on spring-fall curve","off_season_specials":"spring value ski; weekday + night-ski deals; tubing packages; learn-to-ski intro bundles; summer bike-park + scenic-lift calendar as green-season engine","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, US school half-terms; Alpental Plus blackouts = Dec 26 2026-Jan 1 2027 + Sat/Sun Jan 2-Feb 28 2027 + Jan 18 + Feb 16 2027 (verify)","fire_date":"FIRE ski mid-late Mar (ahead of Apr-Jun early-bird/season-pass) + late Aug-early Sep (ahead of Sep-Nov fall wave); push learn-to-ski/night-ski/tubing family layer into Seattle metro from Nov; summer bike park by Apr-May"},"jewels":[{"name":"Point it down Alpental","status":"future","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~USD 79-129/day window; guided/backcountry higher","timing":"ski ~Dec-Apr, snow-dependent; in-area patrolled, beyond-ropes guide-only","draw_rank":1,"hook":"2,280 ft of vertical and some of the steepest lift-served terrai