  ('sunday-river-sugarloaf-maine', '12A', 'Sunday River + Sugarloaf', 'United States', 'Maine''s two big mountains', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'New England', '{"ski","family","culinary","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Sunday River (Newry/Bethel, western Maine) = Boyne (with Sugarloaf since 2007), Ikon + New England Pass; 8 interconnected peaks, ~884 acres, 139 trails, 19 lifts, 2,340-ft vertical (2nd in Maine, 6th in New England); snowmaking ~552 acres (one of the biggest in US skiing); 2008 Chondola out of South Ridge; slopeside Grand Summit (~230 rooms) + premier Jordan Grand; Bethel base town","Sugarloaf (Carrabassett Valley, Rte 27) = Boyne/Ikon/New England Pass; ~1,360 acres = biggest single-mountain ski area in the East (2nd-largest east of the Mississippi after Killington); 162 trails/glades; 2,820-ft continuous vertical (2nd-longest in New England); the ONLY lift-served above-treeline skiing in the Northeast (the Snowfields) + Brackett Basin/Burnt Mountain (650+ acres); slopeside village (Sugarloaf Mountain Hotel + 45 North, Sugarloaf Inn); remote","Both on the Ikon Pass + Boyne''s New England Pass (Gold/Silver/Bronze; with Loon NH + Pleasant Mountain on some tiers)","Nearest ER: Sunday River -> Rumford Hospital (24/7 ER) / Bridgton; Sugarloaf -> Franklin Memorial, Farmington (remote); serious trauma to Portland (Maine Medical Center)","In-bounds lift-served + patrolled — low in-bounds avalanche risk; the real hazards are ice/hardpack, extreme cold/wind-chill (exposed Snowfields) + remote winter driving"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"Sunday River -> Rumford Hospital (24/7 ER, ~25 min) + Bridgton Hospital in range; Sugarloaf -> Franklin Memorial Hospital, Farmington (REMOTE — long drive, significant transfer for serious cases); serious trauma to Portland (Maine Medical Center); ski patrol both mountains; backcountry via county sheriffs + Maine Warden Service / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ICE/HARDPACK + freeze-thaw ''boilerplate'' (defining Eastern condition — sharp edges, respect refreeze); EXTREME COLD + WIND-CHILL (acute — Sugarloaf''s above-treeline Snowfields fully wind-exposed, frostbite fast, upper lifts hold on wind); REMOTE WINTER DRIVING (Rte 2/26 to Sunday River/Bethel, long remote Rte 27 to Sugarloaf; black ice/nor''easters; 511 Maine/newengland511); above-treeline Snowfields (wind slab/firm exposure) + Brackett Basin/Burnt Mountain glades (tree wells); LOW in-bounds avalanche risk","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, Feb school-vacation week) + strong weekend peaks (Boston/New England drive market); Sugarloaf Snowfields window late winter-spring","shoulder":"early season (late Nov-mid Dec — Sunday River snowmaking edge), Jan weekdays, late Mar-Apr spring corn","green":"mid-Apr-May + Oct-mid Nov (between-season lulls; reduced ops — verify); summer golf/biking separate warm-season layer","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + slopeside hotels (Jordan Grand, Sugarloaf Mountain Hotel) + Feb vacation week 3-8 mo; Presidents''/Feb 2-5 mo; spring-corn/shoulder 1-4 wk (drive-in New England market)","off_season_specials":"spring-corn ski deals (late Mar-Apr); early-season pre-Christmas ski (Sunday River snowmaking); summer golf + mountain biking + Carrabassett/Bethel outdoors; midweek value all winter","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, US school half-terms, spring closing/pond-skim/slush-cup (verify 2027)","fire_date":"FIRE ski mid-late Mar (ahead of Apr-Jun early-bird) + lat