  ('telluride-colorado', '12A', 'Telluride', 'United States', 'A Victorian box-canyon town, a free gondola to Mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Colorado Rockies', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","romance","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Telluride = Telski (independent, Epic Pass partner - most full Epic tiers include 7 days); a genuine 1880s Victorian box-canyon mining town (National Historic Landmark, 8,754 ft) + modern Mountain Village (~9,545 ft)","FREE public pedestrian gondola links town and Mountain Village (opened Dec 1996, ~13 min, cresting ~10,540 ft) - a rare free town-to-base lift + ski access","One of the biggest verticals in the US: 4,425 ft total (base 8,725 / summit 13,150; lift-served 3,845 ft); 2,000+ acres; 127 trails; 2 gondolas + 12 chairlifts; terrain ~23 beg/36 int/41 adv; no night skiing","Steep hike-to: Palmyra Peak (~13,320 ft), Gold Hill Chutes, Black Iron Bowl; ~280-330 in snowfall (range)","REAL heli-skiing: Telluride Helitrax (since 1982, ~200 sq mi San Juan terrain, based at The Peaks) - Colorado''s ORIGINAL/most-experienced heli op, NOT the only one (Silverton also flies); NO confirmed Telluride cat operation","Ultra bed base: Madeline Hotel & Residences (Auberge), The Peaks Resort & Spa (Colorado''s largest spa), Lumiere (Dunton), historic-town New Sheridan (1895); Allred''s fine dining atop the gondola (10,551 ft)","Remote/high-spend: MTJ ~65 mi (main jet), TEX ~6 mi (small/weather-dependent), DEN ~330 mi (~6-7 hr); festival town (Bluegrass Jun, Film Festival Sep)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: high-spend, lower-volume, remote by consensus - never hard-state a number; CAIC ''Northern San Juan'' zone; Telluride Medical Center (Level V trauma, region''s only 24/7, air-evac transfers); season 2025-26 27 Nov-5 Apr; NO developed natural hot springs (Ouray/Orvis ~50 mi)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Telluride Medical Center (500 W Pacific Ave) - region''s only 24/7, Level V trauma center; higher-level trauma stabilized + transferred (Montrose/Grand Junction) with air evacuation","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (town ~8,750 ft, Mountain Village ~9,545 ft, ski summit ~13,150 ft, Palmyra ~13,320 ft - AMS real, hike-to adds exertion; acclimatize, hydrate, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE hike-to steeps/heli/backcountry - CAIC ''Northern San Juan'' zone daily bulletin (by ~4:30 PM, complex snowpack), beacon/probe/shovel + operator/guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells; cold + exposed Palmyra hike; remote CO-145/US-550 mountain roads + Traction/Chain Law - check CDOT cotrip.org","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY + Presidents'' Week - ultra-luxury peaks); premium San Juan powder Jan-Feb; summer Bluegrass (Jun) + Film Festival (Sep)","shoulder":"early season (late Nov-mid Dec), Jan midweek, late-Mar/early-Apr spring skiing","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov lull (outside summer festival spikes)","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Madeline/ultra-residences 6-12 mo; Bluegrass + Film Festival lodging 6-12 mo; regular winter 3-6 mo; spring 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"spring skiing; summer festival calendar (Bluegrass, Film, Jazz, Mountainfilm); shoulder ultra-villa value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, Presidents'' Week; summer Telluride Bluegrass (~18-21 Jun 2026), Telluride Film Festival (~4-7 Sep 2026) - verify","fire_date":"FIRE spring early-bird (Mar-Jun) Epic + ultra-lodging pre-book (6-12 mo peak) + festival lodging even earlier; fire again Sep