/Vail_Ski_Resort","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"How do I get to Vail?","a":"**The terrain in numbers:** a **3,450 ft (1,052 m) vertical** from a ~8,120 ft base to an ~11,570 ft summit, split roughly **18% beginner / 29% intermediate / 53% advanced**, served by ~**31–32 lifts** including two gondolas.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vail_Ski_Resort","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Vail?","a":"Cat-ski Vail Pass with Vail Powder Guides — the only USFS-permitted snowcat skiing in the ~4,000-acre Vail Pass Winter Recreation Area — a full day of guided backcountry powder off-mountain.","source":"https://vailpowderguides.com/","accessed":"2026-07-18"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Vail Ski Guide: Colorado''s Largest Mountain, the Back Bowls & Ultra-Luxury","meta_description":"Plan Vail, Colorado - the largest single-mountain ski resort in the state: ~5,300 acres, the legendary Back Bowls, Blue Sky Basin, a purpose-built Bavarian village, true ultra-luxury (Four Seasons, Arrabelle) and Michelin-recognised dining, on the Epic Pass, with real timing, altitude/avalanche safety and booking intel.","slug":"vail-colorado","primary_keyword":"Vail Colorado travel guide","long_tail":["Vail Back Bowls guide","largest ski resort in Colorado","Vail luxury ski-in ski-out hotels","Eagle airport to Vail","Vail Epic Pass","Blue Sky Basin Vail"],"search_language":"es-US","local_keywords":["guia de viaje Vail Colorado","Back Bowls de Vail","la estacion de esqui mas grande de Colorado","hoteles de lujo ski-in ski-out en Vail","Vail Epic Pass","aeropuerto Eagle a Vail"],"hreflang":["en","es-US"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-18","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://sch